<title>JAPAN: N.Korea farm infrastructure needs improvement - FAO.</title>
<headline>N.Korea farm infrastructure needs improvement - FAO.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.N. Food and Agriculture Organisation (FAO) said on Friday that North Korea's agricultural infrastructure needs to be improved in order to solve food shortages there.</p>
<p>&quot;We have started to work beyond food aid. Rehabilitating agricultural infrastracture in North Korea is needed,&quot; FAO director-general Jacques Diouf told reporters in Tokyo.</p>
<p>Diouf said that improvements in grain storage facilities and fertiliser supplies were particularly necessary.</p>
<p>North Korea has been suffering from severe food shortages following two years of devastating floods which washed away a huge acreage of rice paddies.</p>
</text>
